{%- comment -%}
  First reminder – Shopify Email code template (send on 2026-10-12).

  How to use (Shopify admin → Marketing → Shopify Email → Create email → Code):
    1. Run `node index.js usage` first, so customers who already used their card
       carry the OCT26RTPROMO-USED tag and are left out.
    2. Paste this whole file into the code editor (the editor wants a fragment:
       no <!DOCTYPE>, <html>, <head> or <body>; Shopify wraps it).
    3. Right-hand panel:
         To            segment: customer_tags CONTAINS 'OCT26RTPROMO' AND NOT customer_tags CONTAINS 'OCT26RTPROMO-USED'
         Subject       ⏰ TIME IS RUNNING OUT: Your LA Balloons CASH expires Oct. 19th!
         Preview text  If you don't use your credit at LABalloons.com by October 19, 2026, you lose it.
    4. "Send test" to yourself, then schedule or send.

  Shopify Email has no gift_card variables, so this email cannot link to the
  card page; a customer who lost the code is told to reply.
  Dates are written out by hand (10/19/2026) – change them here if the expiry
  date changes. Templates must include {{ unsubscribe_link }} (it renders the
  unsubscribe link itself) and {{ open_tracking_block }}; both are at the end.
  The first name is cut at "(" because some accounts carry a note in it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign promo_name = '' -%}
{%- if customer.first_name != blank -%}{%- assign promo_name = customer.first_name | split: '(' | first | strip -%}{%- endif -%}
<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color: #f7f7f7;">
  <tr>
    <td align="center" style="padding: 24px 12px;">
      <table width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="max-width: 600px; width: 100%; background-color: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e5e5e5;">

        <!-- Header -->
